# EZAuth API — env documentation
#
# ⚠️ This app does NOT need its own .env file.
# All runtime config comes from the ROOT monorepo file:
#   @ezstart/.env.local / .env.staging / .env.production
#
# See /SECRETS.md for the canonical architecture.
#
# Variables consumed by this API (read from root):
#   - MONGO_URL                  → used via getMongoUrl('ezauth')
#   - JWT_SECRET                 → used via getJwtSecret()
#   - OAUTH_STATE_SECRET         → OAuth CSRF state signing
#   - OAUTH_ENCRYPTION_KEY       → AES-256 key for OAuth token storage
#   - GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID           → Google OAuth 2.0
#   - GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET       → Google OAuth 2.0
#   - GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL        → Google OAuth redirect URI
#   - SSO_ALLOWED_REDIRECTS      → comma-separated allow-list for /sso/authorize
#   - ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN    → JWT access token TTL (e.g. 15m, 24h)
#   - COOKIE_DOMAIN              → cross-subdomain auth cookies in prod
#   - REQUIRE_VERIFIED_EMAIL_FOR_SSO
#   - RESEND_API_KEY             → transactional email sender
#   - SENTRY_DSN_EZAUTH          → resolved via getSentryDsn('ezauth')
#
# For vitest, see apps/ezauth/api/.env.test (loaded by vitest.config.ts).
